    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="VoxTerm features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Terminal Sessions</p>

        <h3>Keep more than one connection alive without losing your place</h3>

        <p>
          Start terminal sessions from saved hosts, give sessions their own names,
          minimize them, restore them later, and keep multiple active connections
          available at the same time. VoxTerm preserves the terminal view so your
          buffer remains there when you return to a session.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Multiple Sessions</span>
          <span>Minimize & Restore</span>
          <span>Persistent Buffer</span>
          <span>Saved Commands</span>
          <span>Session Status</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">SSH Hosts</p>

        <h3>Save the machines you connect to again and again</h3>

        <p>
          Store host names, usernames, ports, authentication methods, favorites,
          and connection details so recurring SSH connections are ready when you
          need them instead of being rebuilt from scratch.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Projects</p>

        <h3>Turn recurring terminal work into reusable workspaces</h3>

        <p>
          Create projects for the development work you return to, associate them
          with a host and working directory, add notes, favorite or archive them,
          and keep project-specific commands attached to the workspace.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Saved Commands</p>

        <h3>Keep common commands close instead of retyping them every time</h3>

        <p>
          Store reusable commands for a session or project, add explanations when
          useful, and run them directly from the terminal workflow when you need
          to repeat a familiar task.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Remote Files</p>

        <h3>Move from the shell to the server's files without leaving the session</h3>

        <p>
          Open VoxTerm's SFTP browser directly from a connected terminal session
          to inspect and work with remote files while staying inside the same
          connection and development context.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Terminal Workspace</p>

        <h3>Work like a terminal app without giving up the structure around it</h3>

        <p>
          VoxTerm combines a persistent terminal view with command input, keyboard
          shortcuts, control-key actions, session commands, project commands,
          connection status, current directory context, and remote file access so
          the terminal can stay at the center of the workflow.
        </p>

        <div class="reader-preview">
          <div class="reader-preview-top">
            <span>Session Status</span>
            <strong>Connected</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-bar">
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-meta">
            <span>Terminal</span>
            <span>Commands</span>
            <span>SFTP</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Live Sessions</p>

        <h2>Leave a terminal session and come back without starting over</h2>

        <p>
          VoxTerm keeps active sessions separate from the page you are viewing.
          Minimize a terminal, move through the rest of the app, and restore that
          same session later while keeping the session's connection state and
          persistent terminal buffer available.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="VoxTerm session preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Active Sessions</span>

        <h4>Keep your connections moving.</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Restore</span>
          <strong>Return to an active terminal</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Minimize</span>
          <strong>Keep working elsewhere in VoxTerm</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Disconnect</span>
          <strong>End a connection when you are done</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the VoxTerm experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Home Dashboard</b>
              <small>See recent hosts, sessions, projects, and quick actions</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The Home page brings your recent hosts, active sessions, recent
            projects, and quick actions together so the things you are most likely
            to need are available without digging through the app first.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Session Manager</b>
              <small>Start, restore, disconnect, and remove terminal sessions</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            VoxTerm gives active sessions their own management view where you can
            resume a terminal, disconnect a live connection, remove a session,
            and start a new one from one of your saved hosts.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Password & Key Authentication</b>
              <small>Connect using the authentication method configured for each host</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Saved hosts can use password or key authentication. VoxTerm can remember
            SSH passwords in Keychain when you choose to keep them so repeated
            connections require less setup.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Project Search & Filters</b>
              <small>Keep active, favorite, and archived workspaces organized</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Search projects by name or details and filter them between active,
            favorites, and archived workspaces. Projects can also be duplicated,
            favorited, archived, restored, or deleted from their management view.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Project Commands</b>
              <small>Attach reusable command sets to the work they belong to</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Project-specific commands stay attached to a project so the commands
            you repeatedly use for one workspace can remain separate from
            commands you save for another session or project.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Terminal Controls</b>
              <small>Use mobile-friendly keys and shortcuts while working in the shell</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The terminal includes an accessory toolbar for Done, Ctrl, Esc, Tab,
            saved Commands, and common control characters so terminal work remains
            practical on a touch keyboard.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Themes, Profile & Settings</b>
              <small>Adjust the app around the way you prefer to work</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            VoxTerm includes Profile and Settings areas alongside its primary
            terminal workflow, with theme-aware interface styling used throughout
            the app's hosts, sessions, projects, and terminal experiences.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built Around Real Development Work</p>

        <h2>Your terminal should remember the context around the command line.</h2>

        <p>
          VoxTerm is built around the way development work actually repeats:
          familiar hosts, recurring projects, commands you use again, and sessions
          you may need to leave and restore. Each part gets its own place while
          staying connected to the same terminal-centered workflow.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="https://discord.gg/SaZJKF3d9U">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore VoxTerm</p>

      <h2>Keep your terminal workflow close, organized, and ready to resume.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about VoxTerm, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/VoxTerm/issues/1"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>VoxTerm Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-voxterm-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .voxterm-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .floating-card {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    animation: float 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .floating-card span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .floating-card strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .floating-card-one {
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
  }

  .floating-card-two {
    bottom: 8px;
    left: 0;
    animation-delay: -2.4s;
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) {
    :global(.content:has(.voxterm-page)) {
      max-width: 1280px;
      padding-inline: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    }

    .hero {
      grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 1fr)
        minmax(340px, 380px);
      gap: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 4rem);
      min-height: 610px;
      padding: 2.15rem 0 2.65rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      max-width: 840px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      font-size: 4.15rem;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .hero-text {
      max-width: 660px;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .hero-showcase {
      align-self: center;
      justify-self: end;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 380px;
      min-height: 430px;
    }

    .main-card {
      inset: 58px 16px 104px 16px;
      padding: 1.45rem;
      border-radius: 26px;
      transform: none;
    }

    .main-card h4 {
      max-width: 320px;
      font-size: 2.35rem;
    }

    .progress-line {
      margin: 1.2rem 0;
    }

    .showcase-stats {
      gap: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .floating-card-one {
      top: 0;
      right: 0;
      max-width: 282px;
    }

    .floating-card-two {
      bottom: 16px;
      left: 0;
      max-width: 292px;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) and (max-width: 1160px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 1fr)
        minmax(320px, 340px);
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 3.7rem;
    }

    .main-card h4 {
      font-size: 2.1rem;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1400px) {
    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 4.75rem;
    }
  }

  .intro-section {
    max-width: 850px;
    padding: 4rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .intro-section h2,
  .gallery-heading h2,
  .spotlight h2,
  .details-section h2,
  .community-banner h2,
  .cta-section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .voxterm-gallery-section {
    position: relative;
    padding: 2rem 0 3.25rem;
  }

  .gallery-heading {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .voxterm-gallery {
    position: relative;
    width: min(100%, 430px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 1rem 0 2.75rem;
    touch-action: pan-y;
  }

  .gallery-track-container {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 32px;
  }

  .gallery-track {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    will-change: transform;
    transition:
      transform 0.62s
      cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .gallery-slide {
    flex: 0 0 100%;
    margin: 0;
    opacity: 0.78;
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
  }

  .gallery-slide.is-active {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .gallery-slide img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1170 / 2532;
    object-fit: cover;
